        "Commissioning the Adaptive Process for an O-Ring Linac"
      ],
      "text": "Dr. Xenia Ray Dr. Ray’s research is focused on the development of algorithms to help determine when automated re-planning should be performed in patients undergoing radiotherapy based on changes detected on daily cone-beam CT images. Such algorithms are vital to the optimal clinical implementation of adaptive radiotherapy. She is also working to develop automated tools to facilitate big-data analyses of retrospective clinical data included batch automated replanning via RapidPlan, plan comparison, DVH extraction, and timing data. Explore the Lab People Learn more about the dedicated team in Dr. Xenia Ray's lab. Meet Our Team Publications Explore the latest publications from Dr. Xenia Ray's lab. See Publications Featured Articles Predicting Adaptive Radiotherapy Benefit for Cervical Cancer Patients Evaluating a Physics-Led Adaptive Workflow for Cervical Cancer Commissioning the Adaptive Process for an O-Ring Linac",
